      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A shingle mill by Hewitt and a sash and blind factory by James Smith were early industrial landmarks in Muir.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://villageofmuirmi.gov/a-history-of-muir/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the late 19th century, economic prosperity led to replacing wooden structures with brick buildings, creating the town’s recognizable historic look.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kupi.com/en-ae/explore/united-states/muir/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the second half of the 20th century, Muir had become a quiet residential community that preserves its historic downtown architecture.",
